{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added an optional per-feed polling interval, `refresh_interval` (integer minutes, 0 = use the global interval). The build and all existing unit and integration tests pass; the new behaviour itself has no tests of its own here.\n\nWhat changed:\n- **Migration**: new migration at the end of the list adds `feeds.refresh_interval int not null default 0`.\n- **Model / API**: `Feed.RefreshInterval` appears in the feed JSON as `refresh_interval`; `PUT /v1/feeds/{feedID}` accepts it via `FeedModificationRequest`. The Go client's `Feed` and `FeedModificationRequest` carry the field too (`*int` on the request).\n- **Storage**: the column is read in the feed query and written by `CreateFeed` and `UpdateFeed`.\n- **Scheduler**: `Feed.ScheduleNextCheck` uses the per-feed interval when it is above 0, instead of the round-robin / entry-frequency calculation.\n- **Web UI**: the feed edit form has a number input named `refresh_interval` in the network settings fieldset, pre-filled from the feed and saved on update.\n- **Validation**: negative values (and values above the int32 column range) are rejected with a new error message, in both the API and the UI. A non-numeric value in the web form is rejected rather than silently treated as 0.\n\nBehaviour choices worth knowing:\n- A server-requested delay (Retry-After, feed TTL, Cache-Control, Expires) still wins if it is longer than the per-feed interval. The global maximum-interval clamp is not applied to a per-feed value.\n- Setting a shorter interval pulls `next_check_at` forward, so it takes effect without waiting out the previously scheduled check. This goes through a new `Feed.SetRefreshInterval` helper used by both the API patch and the UI form merge.\n- A web-form submission without the `refresh_interval` field resets the feed to 0 (global), like the form's other fields.\n\nTranslations: the two new keys (`form.feed.label.refresh_interval`, `error.feed_invalid_refresh_interval`) were added to all 24 locale files with English text, since the lo", "t": 1794462577.197}
{"tool": "_result", "name": "finish", "chars": 55, "t": 1794462577.197}
